    function: 'It increases the lever arm of the quadriceps, improves the efficiency of knee extension and protects the anterior knee. It also centralizes the pull of the extensor mechanism.',
    clinical: 'Patellar fractures may be transverse after direct or indirect trauma. It can dislocate laterally, especially with a shallow trochlea or tight lateral retinaculum. Pain at the inferior pole in a growing child suggests Osgood-Schlatter disease at the tibial tuberosity.',
